---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
import Disclaimer from '../../components/Disclaimer.astro';
import AuthorByline from '../../components/AuthorByline.astro';
import { BUSINESS } from '../../data/site';

const title = 'Medicare Advantage Plans (Part C)';
const seoTitle = 'Medicare Advantage Plans in New York and Connecticut';
const description = 'Medicare Advantage bundles hospital, medical and usually drug coverage into one private plan. Often lower premiums, with networks and copays to weigh.';

const serviceSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'Service',
  name: title,
  serviceType: 'Medicare Advantage Plan',
  provider: { '@id': `${BUSINESS.url}/#organization` },
  areaServed: [{ '@type': 'State', name: 'New York' }, { '@type': 'State', name: 'Connecticut' }],
  description,
};
---

<BaseLayout title={title} seoTitle={seoTitle} description={description} schema={serviceSchema}>
  <PageHero
    title={title}
    breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Medicare Plans', href: '/services' }, { label: 'Medicare Advantage' }]}
  />
  <article class="py-14 lg:py-18">
    <div class="container-narrow prose prose-lg max-w-none prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-crst-primary prose-a:text-crst-accent">
      <p class="lead text-xl text-navy-700">Medicare Advantage (Part C) plans are an alternative to Original Medicare, offered by private insurance companies approved by Medicare. They bundle Part A and Part B — and usually Part D drug coverage — into a single plan.</p>
      <h2>What Medicare health plans are</h2>
      <p>
        <a href="https://www.medicare.gov/health-drug-plans/health-plans" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank">Medicare.gov</a> describes
        Medicare health plans as plans that provide your Part A (Hospital Insurance) and Part B (Medical Insurance) benefits, generally
        offered by private companies that contract with Medicare. Medicare Advantage Plans (Part C) are the most common type; the others
        include Medicare Cost Plans, demonstration and pilot programs, and the Program of All-inclusive Care for the Elderly (PACE). This page
        is about Medicare Advantage.
      </p>

      <h2>What to weigh</h2>
      <p>Medicare Advantage plans often have lower monthly premiums, but coverage works through provider networks and a pay-as-you-go structure of copays and coinsurance. That can be a good fit for some people and a poor fit for others. The right answer depends on your doctors, your medications, your budget, and how you prefer to manage risk.</p>
      <h2>Questions to ask about any plan</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Are my doctors and hospitals in the network?</strong> Check each one by name before you enroll.</li>
        <li><strong>Are my medications covered?</strong> Most plans include drug coverage, so check the formulary and the tier for each drug you take.</li>
        <li><strong>What would a heavy-care year cost?</strong> Look at the copays and coinsurance for hospital stays and specialists, not only the monthly premium.</li>
        <li><strong>What extras are included?</strong> Some plans offer benefits Original Medicare doesn’t, like vision, hearing or dental. Ask what each one actually pays.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How it differs from Medigap</h2>
      <p>
        Medicare Advantage replaces Original Medicare with a single private plan, while a <a href="/services/medicare-supplement">Medigap</a>
        plan works alongside Original Medicare and is used with it. The two are different routes, and the choice usually comes down to
        provider freedom against monthly premium and cost-sharing. Read
        <a href="/medicare-advantage-vs-medigap">Medigap vs. Medicare Advantage</a> and
        <a href="/medicare-advantage-pros-and-cons">the pros and cons of Medicare Advantage</a> for the full comparison, and see
        <a href="/medigap-plan-g-cost-new-york">what Medigap Plan G costs in New York</a> if you want the other side of the numbers.
      </p>

      <h2>How I help</h2>
      <p>I’ll walk you through how a specific Medicare Advantage plan compares with a Medicare Supplement approach for your situation — including what each would likely cost you in a healthy year and a heavy-care year — so the decision is based on real numbers, not a sales pitch.</p>

      <AuthorByline />
      <div class="not-prose mt-8"><Disclaimer variant="tpmo" /></div>
    </div>
  </article>
  <CTASection />
</BaseLayout>
